   "text": {
    "L1": "In The Tunnel, Ravi waits near a dark tunnel for the evening train.",
    "L2": "He sees a leopard there, and the glowing eyes make the moment mysterious.",
    "L3": "The darkness, distant sounds, and the word “suddenly” build suspense.",
    "L4": "Words such as “shrieked” and “roared” help us hear the scene and feel its power.",
    "L5": "The leopard is not a villain. It avoids trouble and returns to its home in the forest.",
    "L6": "Articles help us show whether a noun is new or already known.",
    "L7": "We say “an owl” and “a leopard”; later, we say “the owl” and “the leopard.”",
    "L8": "Now choose the phrase with the correct article for owl."
   },
